vior with new examples. Example 3's output order is a reorganization of the inputs. I was getting bogged down in the layout but focused on how each block's output relates to its input. The core concept is becoming clear.\n\n\n**Mapping Block Transitions**\n\nI've been mapping the transitions between input and output blocks in Example 3. I've confirmed that the output blocks are directly related to the input blocks, and that their contents are not modified. The key seems to be the reordering! Specifically, the order of each block *type* in the output matches a block input, in a systematic and predictable way. I have it!\n\n\n**Defining Animation Sequencing**\n\nI've realized the core concept is an *animation*! I'm now certain each example represents a trajectory. I am working to confirm the outputs represent a sequence of the input blocks. Specifically, Example 2 has a bar moving downwards, and Example 1 has a single pixel moving diagonally.\n\n\n",
